    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Low bone mass with high fracture risk by FRAX, starting treatment (M85.89)</content>. 25-hydroxyvitamin D 38 ng/mL, now at target. Calcium 9.5 mg/dL, creatinine 0.8 mg/dL, eGFR 81, and 24-hour urine calcium 172 mg, all normal, so the secondary-causes work-up is complete and shows no cause. Dental examination done. Ready for the first dose. [S]<list><item>Zoledronic acid 5 mg intravenously over 30 minutes in the infusion room today, after a glass of water.</item><item>Acetaminophen 1000 mg every 6 hours as needed for up to three days for the aches or fever that can follow a first dose.</item><item>Continue vitamin D3 2000 units daily and calcium from food.</item><item>Fasting morning CTX and calcium at the six-month visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of falls (Z91.81)</content>. Balance much improved after the program: tandem stance 18 seconds, up from 8; Timed Up and Go 9 seconds, down from 11; no falls. [S]<list><item>Home balance and strength program three times a week.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder in sustained remission (F10.21)</content>. No alcohol or cravings. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone. [S]<list><item>Continue the recovery check at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>25-hydroxyvitamin D</td><td>At baseline; after repletion until 30 ng/mL or more; then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>38 ng/mL, up from 24; at target; next yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Serum calcium before each intravenous antiresorptive dose</td><td>Before each zoledronic acid dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>9.5 mg/dL, normal; infusion given</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Creatinine and eGFR before each zoledronic acid dose</td><td>Before each dose; do not give if creatinine clearance is below 35 mL/min</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Creatinine 0.8 mg/dL, eGFR 81</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>24-hour urine calcium</td><td>At diagnosis, before starting therapy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>172 mg in 24 hours, normal; no hypercalciuria. Deviation: collected about three months after it was ordered, because the sample was missed before the four-week visit. No harm resulted: no drug was started until it was done, and the result is normal. Corrective action: baseline tests that need a home collection are now scheduled with the patient before she leaves the intake visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Bone-turnover marker (fasting serum CTX)</td><td>Baseline, then 3 to 6 months after starting or changing therapy</td><td>Due</td><td>Baseline 560 pg/mL; repeat at the six-month visit, three months after today&apos;s dose</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dental examination before an antiresorptive</td><td>Before starting a bisphosphonate or denosumab</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Routine examination three weeks ago with no problems; no invasive dental work planned</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>First zoledronic acid dose</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>5 mg intravenously over 30 minutes; acetaminophen plan given for the acute-phase reaction</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Central DXA of the spine and hip</td><td>Every 1 to 2 years on therapy until stable, on the same scanner</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Repeat two years after starting therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Standing height by stadiometer</td><td>Yearly; vertebral imaging again if height falls 2 cm or more</td><td>Up to date</td><td>164.0 cm at intake; unchanged on today&apos;s vital signs</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall-risk screen</td><td>Yearly, and with any fall</td><td>Completed today</td><td>After the balance program: Timed Up and Go 9 seconds, tandem stance 18 seconds; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Calcium intake assessment</td><td>At baseline and yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>About 1200 mg a day from food</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Drug-holiday eligibility</td><td>After 3 yearly zoledronic acid doses or 5 years of an oral bisphosphonate</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>First dose today; reassess after the third yearly dose</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Balance and strength exercise program</td><td>With a history of falls or impaired balance</td><td>Completed today</td><td>16 of 16 sessions finished four days ago; home program three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Recovery check (alcohol, cravings, stress)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol; no cravings</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review and safety plan, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in her phone</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Total calcium intake of about 1200 mg a day, mostly from food, by the four-week visit. Outcome by 2026-03-10: About 1200 mg a day from food by her own three-day food record [S]</item><item>25-hydroxyvitamin D of 30 ng/mL or more before the first infusion. Outcome by 2026-05-12: 24 ng/mL at intake and 38 ng/mL at three months [S]</item><item>First zoledronic acid dose by the three-month visit, with normal calcium and kidney function and a dental check done. Outcome by 2026-05-12: Given at three months after normal calcium (9.5 mg/dL) and eGFR (81) and a routine dental examination [S]</item><item>Complete the eight-week balance and strength program, with no falls through six months. In progress; target 2026-08-11 [S]</item><item>Serum CTX at least 30 percent lower three months after the first dose. In progress; target 2026-08-11 [S]</item><item>Sustained remission from alcohol use disorder throughout the episode. In progress; target 2026-08-11 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, osteoporosis monograph (2026); The clinician&apos;s guide to prevention and treatment of osteoporosis (2022); American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists/American College of Endocrinology Clinical Practice Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Postmenopausal Osteoporosis, 2020 Update (2020); Pharmacological Management of Osteoporosis in Postmenopausal Women: An Endocrine Society Clinical Practice Guideline (2019); STEADI: Stopping Elderly Accidents, Deaths, and Injuries (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Zoledronic acid infusion today. Call the clinic for fever lasting more than three days, muscle cramps or tingling, or jaw pain. Six-month bone health review in three months with fasting CTX and calcium. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-11: six-month bone health review, three months after the first infusion. [S]</paragraph></text>

